165 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 98 0 R
/E (Apache locates the requested PHP file in the XAMPP htdocs folder. The PHP code is then processed by the PHP interpreter. If the program needs database information, PHP communicates with MariaDB/MySQL. The result is then returned to Apache, which sends the generated webpage back to the browser. Thus, XAMPP allows the complete interaction between browser, web server, PHP, and database to take place locally. )
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [18]
>>
