197 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (The Laundry Management System is a web-based application developed to help laundry shop owners and staff manage their daily operations efficiently. The system helps track customer details, machine status, service types, orders, and billing in a centralized and organized manner. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
198 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (The main purpose of the project is to digitize traditional laundry shop operations, reducing the need for paper-based records such as notebooks, handwritten slips, and manual billing. Users can visit the website to view machine availability, book washing machines, track order status, manage customers, and generate bills automatically. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
199 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (The project is developed using HTML and CSS for designing and styling the web pages and PHP for implementing the server-side functionality. XAMPP is used as the local development environment, with Apache acting as the web server and MySQL used for storing and managing project data. PHP allows the website to process user requests and display dynamic information. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
200 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 100 0 R
/E (The Laundry Management System aims to make laundry operations simple, organized, and efficient for shop owners. By combining customer management, machine tracking, order booking, and billing features into a single application, the system provides a convenient platform for managing daily laundry activities. )
/Pg 14 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
